Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:48:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] receipts: phase 3 - the user-home path scrub, its re-key
 trap, and the publish commands

User-home hits 114 -> 2 on the export branch; the 2 that remain are upstream's own MyUser/MyUsers placeholders in docs/backend/snapdragon/windows.md. The President's Windows user name appears nowhere on the export branch, in any blob or message. Studio paths untouched by rule: outside the generated series both branches carry the same 18 lines.

Records the trap that would have shipped silently: filter-repo's commit-map is CUMULATIVE, so re-keying the phase-2 output a second time resolves 0 of 415 rows while the originals resolve 415/415. Every ledger was restored from the prep branch and re-keyed ONCE.

Two side-findings added. SF-P6: the bare token <first-name> survives 240 times, almost all in upstream's AUTHORS - out of scope and it should stay so. SF-P7: the phase-2 export sweep was measured between two commits, on a tree no commit ever held, and is corrected here rather than restated.

Also carries the publish commands, written out and NOT run, with the warning that the tag must be re-created in the clone: filter-repo ran with --refs export, so no tag was rewritten and every inherited tag points at pre-rewrite commits.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native) - release engineering for this fork; no upstream origin exists.
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - documents only; no code path is touched.
